Tally Prime Data & XML Architecture: The Complete Reference Guide
Tally Prime organizes data as an object-oriented hierarchical tree rather than relational SQL tables. Below is the full breakdown of how Invoices, Delivery Challans, Stock & Dual Serial Numbers, and Ledgers are structured, calculated, and stored.
1. Ledgers (Parties vs. Accounts)
In Tally, there are no separate tables for customers, suppliers, banks, or taxes. Every entity is a <LEDGER>, and its behavior is dictated entirely by its <PARENT> group:
* Customer: <PARENT>Sundry Debtors</PARENT> (Account Receivable).
* Vendor / Supplier: <PARENT>Sundry Creditors</PARENT> (Account Payable).
* Bank / Cash: <PARENT>Bank Accounts</PARENT> or <PARENT>Cash-in-Hand</PARENT>.
* Tax Accounts: <PARENT>Duties & Taxes</PARENT> (Sub-types: GST \rightarrow CGST, SGST, IGST).
* Revenue / Expense: <PARENT>Sales Accounts</PARENT>, <PARENT>Purchase Accounts</PARENT>, etc.
A. Core Data (Stored in Every Ledger)
* <NAME>: Account / Party name.
* <PARENT>: Group classification.
* <OPENINGBALANCE>: Starting balance.
   * Positive (> 0): Debit (Dr) \rightarrow Asset, Receivable, Expense.
   * Negative (< 0): Credit (Cr) \rightarrow Liability, Payable, Income.
B. Conditional / Extra Data
* <ISBILLWISEON>: Set to Yes for parties to enable invoice-by-invoice aging.
* <LEDGSTREGDETAILS.LIST>: Holds <GSTREGISTRATIONTYPE> (Regular, Unregistered/Consumer), State, and <GSTIN>.
* <LEDMAILINGDETAILS.LIST>: Physical street addresses, State, Country, and PIN code.
* Contact Details: Phone number, PAN (<INCOMETAXNUMBER>), and credit limit terms.
2. Stock Items & Serial Numbers (Single vs. Dual Serial)
Products are defined under <STOCKITEM> and mapped to physical quantities, warehouses, and serial numbers.
A. Core Data (Stored for Every Stock Item)
* <NAME>: Product name / model.
* <PARENT>: Stock Group / category (e.g., Split AC, Copper Piping).
* <BASEUNITS>: Unit of measure (e.g., SET, PCS, NOS).
B. Conditional / Extra Data
* <HSNCODE>: 8-digit HSN code for GST compliance.
* <GSTDETAILS.LIST>: Taxability (Taxable, Exempt) and IGST/CGST/SGST tax slabs.
* <ISBATCHWISEON>: Set to Yes when tracking individual serial or batch numbers.
C. Handling Dual Serial Numbers (IDU & ODU)
Appliances like Split Air Conditioners are sold as 1 SET, but physically consist of two distinct units with separate warranty numbers:
1. IDU (Indoor Unit): The wall-mounted evaporator unit.
2. ODU (Outdoor Unit): The external compressor/condenser cabinet.
In Tally and billing databases, this is handled in two standard ways:
Option 1: Paired Serial String (Single Set Item — Most Common)
The item is billed as 1 SET, and both serials are stored in the <BATCHNAME> tag separated by a delimiter:
<ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST>
<STOCKITEMNAME>1.5 Ton Split AC 5 Star</STOCKITEMNAME>
<ACTUALQTY> 1 SET</ACTUALQTY>
<BILLEDQTY> 1 SET</BILLEDQTY>
<RATE>35000.00/SET</RATE>
<AMOUNT>35000.00</AMOUNT>

<!-- Dual Serial Number Allocation -->
<BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST>
 <GODOWNNAME>Central Warehouse</GODOWNNAME>
 <BATCHNAME>IDU:VOLT-882190 / ODU:VOLT-993412</BATCHNAME>
 <ACTUALQTY> 1 SET</ACTUALQTY>
 <BILLEDQTY> 1 SET</BILLEDQTY>
 <AMOUNT>35000.00</AMOUNT>
</BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST>
</ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST>

Option 2: Component Breakdown (Two Distinct Items)
The invoice includes two separate line items:
* 1.5 Ton AC - Indoor Unit \rightarrow Batch <BATCHNAME>IDU-882190</BATCHNAME> (1 NOS).
* 1.5 Ton AC - Outdoor Unit \rightarrow Batch <BATCHNAME>ODU-993412</BATCHNAME> (1 NOS).
3. Delivery Challan vs. Sales Invoice
Transactions are wrapped in a <VOUCHER>.
Feature
	Delivery Challan (Delivery Note)
	Sales Invoice (Sales)
	Primary Goal
	Physical dispatch / Handover proof
	Commercial billing & tax filing
	Inventory Effect
	Deducts stock immediately from Godown
	Deducts stock immediately from Godown
	Financial Ledgers
	None. <ALLLEDGERENTRIES.LIST> is empty
	Debits Customer, Credits Sales & Tax
	P&L / Balance Sheet
	No change in financial statements
	Directly updates sales revenue & GST payable
	Bill Balance
	No pending payment recorded
	Creates an active pending New Ref bill
	A. Delivery Challan Structure
Contains only header info and <ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST> with the godown and serial numbers:
<VOUCHER VCHTYPE="Delivery Note" Action="Create">
<DATE>20261015</DATE>
<VOUCHERNUMBER>DC/001/26-27</VOUCHERNUMBER>
<PARTYLEDGERNAME>Metro Cooling Center</PARTYLEDGERNAME>

<ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST>
 <STOCKITEMNAME>1.5 Ton Split AC 5 Star</STOCKITEMNAME>
 <ACTUALQTY> 1 SET</ACTUALQTY>
 <BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST>
  <GODOWNNAME>Central Warehouse</GODOWNNAME>
  <BATCHNAME>IDU:VOLT-882190 / ODU:VOLT-993412</BATCHNAME>
  <ACTUALQTY> 1 SET</ACTUALQTY>
 </BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST>
</ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST>
</VOUCHER>

B. Sales Invoice Structure (Zero-Sum Balancing)
Contains both financial lines and inventory lines. Across <ALLLEDGERENTRIES.LIST>, the amounts must mathematically sum to zero (\sum = 0):
* Customer Debit (-41,300.00): Grand total receivable (Base 35,000 + 18% GST).
* Sales Credit (35,000.00): Taxable goods revenue.
* Output CGST Credit (3,150.00): 9% Central tax liability.
* Output SGST Credit (3,150.00): 9% State tax liability.
* Attached Inventory Lines: Product rate, quantity, warehouse, and dual serial numbers (IDU/ODU) matching the billed units.
4. Quick Field-by-Field Reference
Goal
	Where to Look in Tally XML
	Check Customer Dues
	<LEDGER> where parent is Sundry Debtors \rightarrow inspect <OPENINGBALANCE> and <BILLALLOCATIONS.LIST>.
	Read Invoice Total & Tax
	<VOUCHER VCHTYPE="Sales"> \rightarrow inspect party row and tax rows inside <ALLLEDGERENTRIES.LIST>.
	Track AC Serial (IDU/ODU)
	Inside <ALLINVENTORYENTRIES.LIST> \rightarrow <BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST> \rightarrow <BATCHNAME>.
	Warehouse Location
	Inside <BATCHALLOCATIONS.LIST> \rightarrow <GODOWNNAME>.